From: appkins <nbatkins@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 22 Aug 2026 12:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] DwUsbHostDxe: report the real port speed and stop splitting on
 the root port

DwHcGetRootHubPortStatus never read HPRT0.PRTSPD. DWC2_HPRT0_PRTSPD_MASK is
defined in DwcHw.h and referenced by no .c file in the driver; the function
set USB_PORT_STAT_HIGH_SPEED unconditionally, so every device on the root
port was reported to UsbBusDxe as high speed no matter what the core had
actually negotiated.

On BCM283x this was invisible: the DWC2 there is behind the on-board hub, so
the root port always trains at high speed and the hardcoded answer happened
to be right. The Pi 5 exposes the core directly on the USB-C connector, where
a full- or low-speed device trains the port at its own speed and the reported
value becomes a lie -- UsbBusDxe then picks transfer sizes and timings for a
link that is not there.

Reporting the speed honestly is not sufficient on its own. DwHcTransfer turns
on split transactions for any low- or full-speed device, which is correct only
when the device sits behind a high-speed hub's transaction translator. A
device directly on the root port has no TT, and DwOtgHcInit would program
HCSPLT from a zeroed translator (hub address 0, port 0). Until now that path
was unreachable, because the speed was always reported as high; fixing the
speed makes it reachable, so gate splitting on there actually being a
translator. UsbBusDxe always passes a non-NULL pointer -- USB_DEVICE embeds
the struct by value -- so the meaningful test is TranslatorHubAddress != 0,
device address 0 never being a valid hub address.

The one-shot DEBUG_ERROR reports the negotiated speed once per change rather
than on every poll, so a port that trains at the wrong speed says so in the
log instead of being inferred from downstream transfer failures.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: appkins <nbatkins@gmail.com>
---
--- a/Platform/RaspberryPi/Drivers/DwUsbHostDxe/DwUsbHostDxe.c
+++ b/Platform/RaspberryPi/Drivers/DwUsbHostDxe/DwUsbHostDxe.c
@@ -305,8 +305,9 @@
 
   do {
   RestartXfer:
-    if (DeviceSpeed == EFI_USB_SPEED_LOW ||
-        DeviceSpeed == EFI_USB_SPEED_FULL) {
+    if ((DeviceSpeed == EFI_USB_SPEED_LOW ||
+         DeviceSpeed == EFI_USB_SPEED_FULL) &&
+        (Translator != NULL) && (Translator->TranslatorHubAddress != 0)) {
       Split.Splitting = TRUE;
       Split.SplitStart = TRUE;
       Split.Tries = 0;
@@ -653,6 +654,8 @@
   return Status;
 }
 
+STATIC UINT32 mLastPortSpeed = 0xFFFFFFFF;
+
 EFI_STATUS
 EFIAPI
 DwHcGetRootHubPortStatus (
@@ -663,6 +666,7 @@
 {
   DWUSB_OTGHC_DEV *DwHc;
   UINT32          Hprt0;
+  UINT32          PortSpeed;
 
   if (PortNumber > DWC2_HC_PORT) {
     return EFI_INVALID_PARAMETER;
@@ -702,7 +706,31 @@
     PortStatus->PortStatus |= USB_PORT_STAT_POWER;
   }
 
-  PortStatus->PortStatus |= USB_PORT_STAT_HIGH_SPEED;
+  //
+  // Report the speed the core actually negotiated. HPRT0.PRTSPD is
+  // authoritative after the port reset completes; hardcoding high speed
+  // told UsbBusDxe the wrong thing for every full- and low-speed device,
+  // which then sized transfers and picked timings for a link that is not
+  // there. 0 = high, 1 = full, 2 = low (DWC2 databook, HPRT0.PRTSPD).
+  //
+  PortSpeed = (Hprt0 & DWC2_HPRT0_PRTSPD_MASK) >> DWC2_HPRT0_PRTSPD_OFFSET;
+  switch (PortSpeed) {
+  case DWC2_HPRT0_PRTSPD_HIGH:
+    PortStatus->PortStatus |= USB_PORT_STAT_HIGH_SPEED;
+    break;
+  case DWC2_HPRT0_PRTSPD_LOW:
+    PortStatus->PortStatus |= USB_PORT_STAT_LOW_SPEED;
+    break;
+  default:
+    break;                    /* full speed sets neither bit */
+  }
+
+  if ((Hprt0 & DWC2_HPRT0_PRTCONNSTS) && (PortSpeed != mLastPortSpeed)) {
+    mLastPortSpeed = PortSpeed;
+    DEBUG ((DEBUG_ERROR, "DwUsbHostDxe: port speed %a (HPRT0 %08x)\n",
+      (PortSpeed == DWC2_HPRT0_PRTSPD_HIGH) ? "high" :
+      (PortSpeed == DWC2_HPRT0_PRTSPD_LOW)  ? "low" : "full", Hprt0));
+  }
 
   if (Hprt0 & DWC2_HPRT0_PRTENCHNG) {
     //              PortStatus->PortChangeStatus |= USB_PORT_STAT_C_ENABLE;
--- a/Platform/RaspberryPi/Drivers/DwUsbHostDxe/DwcHw.h
+++ b/Platform/RaspberryPi/Drivers/DwUsbHostDxe/DwcHw.h
@@ -530,6 +530,9 @@
 #define DWC2_HPRT0_PRTTSTCTL_OFFSET                     13
 #define DWC2_HPRT0_PRTSPD_MASK                          (0x3 << 17)
 #define DWC2_HPRT0_PRTSPD_OFFSET                        17
+#define DWC2_HPRT0_PRTSPD_HIGH                          0
+#define DWC2_HPRT0_PRTSPD_FULL                          1
+#define DWC2_HPRT0_PRTSPD_LOW                           2
 #define DWC2_HAINT_CH0                                  (1 << 0)
 #define DWC2_HAINT_CH0_OFFSET                           0
 #define DWC2_HAINT_CH1                                  (1 << 1)
